id=a52sxq_gallery_slowmo
name=Galaxy A52s 5G: hold a video in Gallery to play it in slow motion
author=kusti420
description=Samsung Gallery's Instant Slow-mo (hold a playing video) is gated on SEC_FLOATING_FEATURE_CAMERA_SUPPORT_AIFRC and plays through SemMediaPlayer.setVideoFrc() -> libaplayer -> the vendor MPP HAL's AI frame rate conversion pipe (libmppaifrc + SNPE 2.x models). The A52s vendor (MPP HAL V1, SNPE 1.x) has no such pipe and the S26 Ultra one cannot run on it, so the feature is stripped. This patch brings the gesture back without interpolation and without touching the Gallery APK (it stays Samsung-signed and Galaxy Store updatable): inside the Gallery process only, SemFloatingFeature reports the feature and its limits, and SemMediaPlayer.setVideoFrc() turns "scale up at rate R" into plain playback at speed R (0.25x while held, back to 1x on release). The real floating_feature.xml is unchanged, so Camera, MotionPhoto, Video Player and libaplayer itself keep their non-AIFRC paths.
